  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening resilience of Afro, indigenous and mestizo communities in Choc&#xF3; affected by COVID19</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to accompany the reconstruction of the socio-economic fabric of 500 families and to contribute to the resilience of Afro descendant, Indigenous and metizo communities in the Diocese of Quibd&#xF3;, who have been and continue to be affected by the effects of the COVID19 post-pandemic, seeking to improve their quality of life, and their family and community life projects. The Diocese of Quibdo is located in the Choco Department, where 6 out of 10 inhabitants face extreme monetary poverty. It is an area that continues to be affected by the ongoing armed conflict and is also prone to climate emergencies. The long-term impacts of COVID-19 pandemic are exacerbated by these factors and especially vulnerable households.
The project has a specific component responding to the emergency of the acute lack of food security for 500 families, along with a more long term approach to strengthen the resilience of Afro descendant, Indigenous and Metizo communities seeking improved income and/or food production levels and positively impact their communities through income generating initiatives and well as seeking changes in public policies through advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
